# NOTE: no `* -merge` here. That rule belongs to the BUS (single-writer
# discipline; conflicts are re-derived, never text-merged — PROTOCOL §3.2) and
# ships in bus-skeleton/.gitattributes. The product is ordinary software,
# maintained with normal git workflows, so normal text merges apply.

# Git LFS: broad binary-blob coverage. Text formats (svg, obj, gltf, csv, json,
# yaml, md) are intentionally excluded so they stay diffable.

# Images
*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
